<title>USA: Georgia jobless rate dips to 4.9 percent in July.</title>
<headline>Georgia jobless rate dips to 4.9 percent in July.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia's unemployment rate dipped to 4.9 percent in July from five percent in June and 5.5 percent a year ago, state Labor Commissioner David Poythress said Friday.</p>
<p>The state gained 27,200 jobs in July, putting total nonfarm employment at a record 3.59 million.</p>
<p>First-time jobless claims rose by 11,702 in July, to 37,267. The total number of people drawing unemployment benefits rose by 13,175 to 56,238 in July.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
